# Design system

Source of truth: [docs/design-system.md](../../docs/design-system.md)

- v1 has **no UI surface**; this rule stays inert until UI code is added under `components/**` or `**/*.tsx`.
- If you are adding a UI surface, you are also adding scope: pause and write a v2 trigger entry in `docs/design-system.md` before merging.
- When UI does land: tokens follow DTCG v1 (Style Dictionary), primitives use shadcn/ui + Base UI / Radix, Storybook ships with `addon-a11y`, visual baselines via Playwright `toHaveScreenshot()`.
- Until then: tool descriptions, OAuth consent strings, and README copy are the only "design surfaces" — keep them plain, short, and screen-reader friendly.
